 Iterative statements :
     1)while
     2) do while ---->entry-controlled loop
     3)for loop -----> exit-controlled loop

1. while loop :
          in while loop first it checks the conditions,if the condition is true
          it execute the block of statement.
          if the condition is false it cant go inside the loop.

     while(condition){
        // block of statement
          }

      EG :
        let n = 1;
       while(n<=10){
        console.log(n);
          n++;----> increamenting.
        }
-----------------------------------------------------------------
2.Do While loop :
      First it execute the statement then it checks the condition.
      atleast it runs the loop one time.
     execute the statement then check the conditions.

     Syntax :
           do {
              // block of statement
            }while(conditions)

3.for loop :
        syntax :
            for(initialization ; condition ; increament/decreament){
                  //block of statement
             }
      











